    "result_text": "Done. The change is implemented and all tests pass.\n\n## What I did\n\n**`AuditOwnerCreated`** now emits the structured event in addition to the existing audit line:\n- Added a `static final AtomicLong SEQ` so `seq` increases monotonically across all creates (thread-safe via `incrementAndGet()`).\n- Extracted a `primaryIdentifier(Owner)` helper that returns `owner.getCustomerCode()` today \u2014 the single point to change when the customerCode is unified into the memberId, so the event will then carry the memberId with no other edits.\n\n**`OwnerCreatedEvent`** (new) \u2014 an immutable Java `record` holding `seq`, `ownerId`, `identifier`, `membershipLevel`, with `toJson()` rendering the canonical, field-ordered object `{seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event:'OWNER_CREATED'}`. The `identifier` value is emitted under the `customerCode` JSON key to match the published contract, with proper JSON string escaping.\n\nThe emitted line, confirmed in the test run:\n```\n{\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\n## Test results\n- `AcceptanceTest.coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier` (the new event assertion) \u2014 passes.\n- Full suite: **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.\n\nOne design note for later: the `identifier`\u2192memberId switch is localized to `primaryIdentifier(...)`, but the JSON key stays literally `customerCode` per the current contract \u2014 you'll likely want to rename that key when the memberId unification lands.",
